+        "description": "Folded leaflet printing from 10 pcs at $0.80. Bi-fold, tri-fold (C/Z), map fold structures; 157-250gsm coated stocks with automatic creasing over 200gsm. Free fold proof, 3-5 day turnaround.",
+        "h1": "Folded Leaflet Printing — Fold Structures, Stock Weight & Reading Flow Guide",
+        "keywords": ["folded leaflet printing","tri-fold leaflets","bi-fold printing","z-fold leaflet","c-fold brochure","leaflet printing","flyer printing hong kong"],
+        "body": "Folded leaflet printing transforms a single printed sheet into a multi-panel format through mechanical folding: one A4 sheet becomes six information panels as a tri-fold — three times the capacity of a flat flyer — while the physical act of unfolding creates a reading ritual of its own. Unlike flat flyers, which are scanned in one glance, or posters, which are read from a distance, the core design challenge of a leaflet is not aesthetics but information hierarchy: what goes on the cover to trigger opening, what goes inside for deep reading, and what goes on the back to drive action. ZprintPro prints folded leaflets from 10 pcs at HK$0.70, serving healthcare patient education, financial product literature, restaurant menus and property brochures.\n\n## Six Fold Structures and Their Capacity\n\n| Fold Type | Panels | Flat Size (A4 finished) | Capacity | Best For |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Half-fold (bi-fold) | 4 | A4→A3 | 2-3 points | Simple promos, invitations, menus |\n| Tri-fold (C-fold) | 6 | 297×630mm | 4-6 points | Product briefs, corporate intros |\n| Tri-fold (Z-fold) | 6 | 297×630mm | 4-6 points | Timelines, process flows, maps |\n| Quad-fold (accordion) | 8 | 297×840mm | 6-8 points | Detailed catalogs, multi-product intros |\n| Map fold | 8-16 | Custom | Extensive charts | Maps, floor plans, large catalogs |\n| Cross fold | 8 | A4→A2 | Center image + surround | Poster-style leaflets, event programs |\n\n## C-Fold vs Z-Fold: The Most Common Dilemma\n\nBoth are tri-folds with six panels and identical flat sizes, but the reading experience differs completely. A C-fold wraps two panels inward, so the reader opens it layer by layer with a sense of reveal — the cover stays whole and branding stays strong, suiting a \"problem first, solution revealed\" narrative. A Z-fold alternates direction, so everything appears at once like an accordion — ideal for parallel comparison, timelines, step diagrams and maps. Choose suspense or full overview.\n\n## Paper Weight vs Fold Compatibility (The Critical Constraint)\n\nThe first constraint in leaflet stock selection is not hand-feel but foldability. 80-128gsm folds freely in any structure; 157gsm folds smoothly up to a tri-fold, but quad-folds need creasing; 200gsm should be limited to bi-fold or tri-fold and must be creased; 250gsm barely manages a bi-fold and needs creasing plus lamination; 300gsm and above should not be folded at all — switch to a saddle-stitched booklet. Creasing compresses a groove at the fold line with a steel rule so fiber breaks stay controlled and the coating does not crack white; any stock at 200gsm or above, or any laminated sheet, must be creased. The cost is already included in the folding operation.\n\n## Reading Flow Design: A Tri-Fold Example\n\nThe six panels are not isolated blocks but a sequenced reading journey. Panel 1 (the cover, visible when folded) must earn the open — hero visual, one-line hook, logo. Panel 2 states the reader's pain point or question. Panel 3 delivers the solution and core value proposition. Panel 4 provides evidence — data, testimonials, certifications. Panel 5 (inner back flap) drives action — promo code, QR code, contact details. Panel 6 (the back cover, also visible when folded) closes the brand — logo, slogan, address. The two exposed panels are free real estate, working like a mini poster at no extra cost.\n\n## Three ZprintPro Differentiators\n\nFirst, a free physical fold proof before mass production — confirming fold direction, panel sequence and crease positions, eliminating batch disasters like reversed folds. Second, automated folding with manual spot checks at fixed intervals for accurate panel registration. Third, one-stop finishing: folding, saddle-stitching, hole punching and numbering in a single run. Standard turnaround is 3-5 working days; WhatsApp +86 198 8085 1334 for advice, or try the [30-second AI quote](/en/quote/). See also: the [flyer printing guide](/en/category/flyers/) for flat messaging of five points or fewer, the [poster printing guide](/en/category/posters/) for distance display, and [menu printing](/en/category/menus/) if your leaflets are restaurant menus."
